valve has teamed up with Taiwanese  smartphone maker HTC and they've  unveiled their virtual reality headset  vibe which uses valves new VR technology  although the announcement comes coupled  with a slightly melodramatic trailer  that looks like the start of a sci-fi  movie before the technology in question  rises up against mankind this one could  be very cool the device has a 1200 x  1800 pixel screen for each eye and a  refresh rate of 90 frames per second  which allegedly eliminates the jitter  that is common with other VR headsets  the vibe also features a gyro sensor  accelerometer and a laser position  sensor that will track the rotation of  your head and if you pair the device  with two steam VR base stations your  movement around the room can also be  tracked the vive headset will come with  a custom controller and the device is  due out this year given that vibe is  powered by valve steam VR the device  will have access to sting games that  utilize we are a bunch of developers  have signed on to make content for the  device including the room developer  fireproof games also signing honor a  studio called alchemy labs who are  developing a game called job simulator  which appears to be like surgeon  simulator with less scalpel and more  foodstuffs but you can see it for  yourself on gamespot let me know down in  the comments if you're keen for valves  entry into VR we'll keep you updated on  this one so stay tuned to gamespot  you
 

